course: dictionary
lesson: 5260
title: Names that become words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A capital letter at the start of a word often means a name. «Jonah was sent to warn Nineveh but ran away on a ship.» Jonah is a person in a Bible story, so here it is a proper noun.
explain: Sometimes a name turns into an ordinary word written with a small letter. A jonah means a person thought to bring bad luck, especially on a ship. Context helps you spot which meaning is used, so ask: is this a person in a story, or an unlucky person?
explain: Look for clues around the word. «Jonah preached, the whole city of Nineveh repented, and God spared it» tells you about a Bible story. Words like ship, sea and sailors often point to the old, informal meaning, so check the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Jonah is a prophet in the Bible who ran away from God's command.
fact: In the story, Jonah was swallowed by a great fish, and after three days he was spat out on land.
fact: The Bible says "a great fish", but many people call the story "Jonah and the whale".
fact: The story teaches that you cannot hide from God and that God shows mercy, even to enemies who change their ways.
fact: A jonah, with a small letter, is an old informal word for a person thought to bring bad luck, especially on a ship.
exercise: «Jonah was sent to warn Nineveh but ran away on a ship.» Who is Jonah? | A city by the sea | *A prophet in a Bible story who ran away from God's command | A great fish that swallowed a sailor | A captain who always won
exercise: Sam says, «Don't sail with him, he's a jonah, everything goes wrong when he's on board.» What does a jonah mean? | A fish that lives in the sea | A famous ship's captain | *A person thought to bring bad luck
exercise: Find the name of a city in this sentence: «Jonah preached, the whole city of Nineveh repented.» | Jonah | preached | *Nineveh | repented
test: Why does the capital J in «Jonah» tell you something? | It shows the word is a fish | *It shows Jonah is a name of a person | It shows the word is the first word of a sad poem | It shows the word means bad luck
test: «Christians differ on whether to read Jonah as history or as a teaching story; this is disputed.» What does disputed mean here? | *Argued about, with people not agreeing | Proved true for certain | Written down by a sailor | Forgotten by everyone
exam: «The sailors blamed the quiet man on the ship: "He's a jonah, we've had bad luck since he came aboard."» What does jonah mean in this sentence? | A great fish | *An unlucky person | A prophet from the Bible | A kind captain
